# M28.bug10 — build-time stub (NO secrets).
#
# Loaded by Next.js when NODE_ENV=production at BUILD time. NOT loaded
# at runtime by next-intl / i18n / logger / most server code (Next.js
# caches env at build, but `process.env.DATABASE_URL` is read at request
# time, which falls through to whatever .env / shell has).
#
# DATABASE_URL is intentionally ABSENT here. The build collects page
# data from each route handler; if any of them reach env.DATABASE_URL
# at build time, they fall through to whatever .env has (or undefined
# — env.ts's Zod parse will throw on DATABASE_URL being missing).
#
# That's fine because the deploy flow mandates running `npm run init`
# BEFORE `npm run build`. Init copies .env.example → .env and flushes
# the operator's shell-supplied DATABASE_URL into it, so by the time
# build runs, .env has a real DATABASE_URL and the build succeeds.
#
# Why not just put the stub URL here? Because at runtime
# `NODE_ENV=production npm run start:server` ALSO loads
# .env.production, and a stub URL there means the server happily
# boots but every DB-touching route 500s with auth failure against
# the stub. Better to fail fast at build time than to silently serve
# 500s in production.
PORT=5002
LOG_LEVEL=info
SESSION_SECRET=build-time-stub-32-chars-min-padding-aaaaa
NODE_ENV=production